        "content": "<p>I noticed that draft PRs get the following message from bors:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">This</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pull</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">request</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">now</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">draft</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mode</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">No</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">active</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">state</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">needed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cleanup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">While</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PR</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">remains</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">draft</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">will</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ignore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">commands</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PR</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mark</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">it</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ready</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">review</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">before</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">commands</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">like</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">or</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bors</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">try</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is unnecessary, because one would only make a draft PR if it is not ready for bors yet. Could this be removed?</p>",
        "id": 591389163,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777384275
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If I remember correctly, I added this after there was some confusing behavior related to PRs being turned into drafts when they were on the queue or after being delegated. I can try and make bors less noisy here, but I do want to point out that the message is not entirely unnecessary, the <code>bors try</code> command could conceivably be used on draft PRs but gets ignored due to the way the command system works.</p>",
        "id": 591394025,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryan Gin-ge Chen",
        "timestamp": 1777385207
    }
]